# Grants the GitHub Actions runner's own user passwordless sudo for
# exactly these three fixed scripts -- nothing else. Each script
# validates its own arguments strictly before touching anything (see
# their own header comments in deploy/sudo/) -- that validation, not
# an argument-pinning sudoers rule, is deliberately what stands between
# an approval-gated but still-untrusted PR branch and root access to
# nginx/systemd on this machine. See deploy/README.md's "Why sudo is
# scoped this way" for the reasoning.
#
# Install (after replacing RUNNER_USER below with the actual account
# the runner service runs as):
#   visudo -cf deploy/sudo/sudoers.d/orbit-viewer   # validate first
#   sudo install -o root -g root -m 0440 \
#     deploy/sudo/sudoers.d/orbit-viewer /etc/sudoers.d/orbit-viewer
RUNNER_USER ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/local/bin/orbit-viewer-deploy-preview.sh, /usr/local/bin/orbit-viewer-teardown-preview.sh, /usr/local/bin/orbit-viewer-deploy-prod.sh
